--TEST--
`$x is $cls` is refused, because the right-hand side of `is` is a type and a variable names a value — `instanceof` is the dynamic class test (`rule:types/type-test`, `rule:types/class-reference-sites`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The right-hand side of `is` is a type, and a variable there names a value
// rather than one.
class Animal {}

mixed $pet = new Animal();
string $cls = "Animal";
echo $pet is $cls, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0812]: the right-hand side of `is` is a type, not a value
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
